                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ed82f9f-3603-3798-9708-759b8f4f1984",
                        "entry_id": "9027eede-5d55-3e10-a9c3-385c03e9a378",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Cesser de détester."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "acccb923-f4cc-4dc1-a353-cd2239778030",
                                "sense_id": "3ed82f9f-3603-3798-9708-759b8f4f1984",
                                "text": "Par exemple, un enfant a dit à sa mère, « I hate you ! And I’ll never unhate you or nothing » (je te déteste ! et je ne te dédétesterai jamais !)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ff0fe7a-99a8-4398-bb6c-372415cd6d59",
                                "sense_id": "3ed82f9f-3603-3798-9708-759b8f4f1984",
                                "text": "Par exemple, le même enfant qui a juré ne jamais « unhate » (dédétester) sa mère récitait une histoire de fantômes huit mois plus tard et disait, « He tippitoed to the graveyard and unburied her » (il marcha sur la pointe des pieds jusqu’au cimetière et la désenterra)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9aadfe4c-0d64-4687-8577-ea3c563c779b",
                                "sense_id": "3ed82f9f-3603-3798-9708-759b8f4f1984",
                                "text": "on doit se dédétester après s’être haïs."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "28ba4d00-2518-45ff-b3dd-3208b8fb485d",
                        "source_entry_id": "9027eede-5d55-3e10-a9c3-385c03e9a378",
                        "source_sense_id": "3ed82f9f-3603-3798-9708-759b8f4f1984",
                        "target_lang_word": "unhate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unhate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eefb094e-cdf5-3224-9bdc-3ffec9b55c76",
                                        "entry_id": "04919c11-3704-3d9a-8c43-2b9713b984b2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To leave off, cease, or desist from hating."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98320680-cff4-4277-9b4c-939496dda51b",
                                                "sense_id": "eefb094e-cdf5-3224-9bdc-3ffec9b55c76",
                                                "text": "I hate you! And I'll never unhate you or nothing!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "441e3aef-28c2-4454-96a7-bfcaf52d84b7",
                                                "sense_id": "eefb094e-cdf5-3224-9bdc-3ffec9b55c76",
                                                "text": "Till when, All that was, is; and must forever be. Nor is it in me to unhate my hates, — [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2230a393-b7a6-4036-ba3d-d8ca7c4c0cad",
                                                "sense_id": "eefb094e-cdf5-3224-9bdc-3ffec9b55c76",
                                                "text": "I learned how to unhate Bush the only way people ever really learn things—by doing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "unhate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2df78ea5-3974-3151-a1cb-0dc5568e178c",
                                        "entry_id": "cc3e49ac-c1a7-310c-bd74-0021f5228c43",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The lack, absence, or omission of hate; hatelessness; love."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9329de3c-4ef1-472c-889d-88d590d4d42b",
                                                "sense_id": "2df78ea5-3974-3151-a1cb-0dc5568e178c",
                                                "text": "Hold me. I am perishing. Achilles We can never perish. It is Unlove and unhate that give form To phantasms of time and space."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78e2629c-c378-4fb9-9636-4d7fe97abae1",
                                                "sense_id": "2df78ea5-3974-3151-a1cb-0dc5568e178c",
                                                "text": "[...] as Greene in his Our Man in Havana and other novels of power and glory, puzzled and worried, for other reasons than purely political or literary, why on earth should lt be easy to work up the politics of hate, but difficult to work out the politics of unhate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
